  "Question": "If the line \\(L\\) in the \\(xy\\)-plane has half the slope and twice the \\(y\\)-intercept of the line \\(y=\\frac23x+4,\\) then an equation for \\(L\\) is",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(y=\\frac13x+8\\)",
    "B": "\\(y=\\frac43x+2\\)",
    "C": "\\(y=\\frac13x+4\\)",
    "D": "\\(y=\\frac43x+4\\)",
    "E": "\\(y=\\frac13x+2\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "A",
  "Solution": "In the form \\(y=mx+b\\), \\(m\\) is the slope and \\(b\\) is the \\(y\\)-intercept. Thus the given line has slope \\(\\frac23\\) and \\(y\\)-intercept \\(4\\).\n\nFor line \\(L\\), the slope and intercept must be\n\\[\nm=\\frac12\\cdot\\frac23=\\frac13,\n\\qquad b=2\\cdot4=8.\n\\]\nPutting these into \\(y=mx+b\\) gives\n\\[\n\\boxed{y=\\frac13x+8},\n\\]\nwhich is choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{A}}\\).",
